# The chaos soak's journal: metrics.jsonl, events.jsonl, repro.log,
# config.json, the per-panel frame dumps and the trip records. Written by
# every soak run, uploaded as a CI artifact, and never committed — a green
# run's journal is a baseline for reading the next red run's slopes, not a
# thing the repository carries.
#
# The repository root already ignores `build/`, so this rule is not what keeps
# the directory out of a commit. It is here because it is the package that
# creates the directory, and the rule that lands in the same commit as the
# first writer is the rule somebody finds when they wonder what build/soak is.
build/soak/
